SWEET AMP DSP MPU (patch 0383, plan A9g), on top of 0382 (boot-arg sweetaoc=6 + sweetamp=1): run a9f loaded and read back the wmfw + .bin on
both amps, then stopped L in the MPU step of amp_dsp_start with no detail. The MPU sequence and the 20 access words match stock exactly
(AMP wm_adsp.c:3098-3126, :246-265; Linux v6.18 cs_dsp.c:2626-2655, :219-245; cs35l41.h:365-391; lock_regions 0xFFFFFFFF cs35l41.c:3728),
and every pair is in the write allowlist. The one non-stock step was ours: the 20 words were read back and compared to 0xFFFFFFFF, which
neither driver does (the words are readable + volatile, cs35l41-tables.c:433-459, :716, but only the VIO words are ever read, wm_adsp.c:4486,
:4515). sweet_amp_dsp.h: the read-back is now a logged value ("SWEET AMP DSP: L|R mpu rb 20/20 not-ffffffff=N [first REG=VAL]"), not a stop;
a refused (allowlist) or failed (SPI / CS) write or read still stops, and a failed write after the unlock sends LOCK_CONFIG := 0 once (the
stock lock value) so the MPU is not left unlocked. Every start / run stage stop now prints "SWEET AMP DSP: L|R step=<sub-step> reg=R w=W
r=V e=0|1|2|ref pwr1=P" (pre-checks, unlock1/2, access, lock, access-read, ccm-start, ccm-en, mbox2-read, hb0-read, hb-read/wN,
hb-still/wN, post-*/wN). Nothing else written to the amps changes; PWR_CTRL1 stays refused; no mailbox command. No Linux code copied.
Host test shim/amp_xnu_host_test.c (MPU words reading back other values: logged, core started, pass line; detail lines). BUILT, UNRUN.

